 "meta": {
   "purpose": "FIRE parity golden (FIRE plan §4.2, R0, F10). fire.ts, retiring at month 0 with tax 0 and no retirement income, must reproduce the reference model on every case below.",
   "model": "The reference model behind FIRE plan §1.3: the 2026-10-05 session's clean-room oracle.mjs (replay, capacity), recovered from that session's transcript on 2026-10-25. Re-run on Node 22.22.2 it reproduces every figure of plan Appendix A — whose rounded figures were read off the live Compass page — including the 2017 and 2021 replays running out in year 8 and year 9 (static 25%) and in year 14 / lasting (power law), and capacity $4,012.52 and $5,383.73. Generalised to an explicit price path and a given monthly factor, as that session did for M2, it is bit-identical to the oracle on those inputs (every month's portfolio, the lowest point and the capacity).",
   "rules": "Each month e: when e > 0 and e % 12 === 0 the withdrawal is multiplied by (1 + inflation). Start of month: portfolio = btc × price[e] + other. If portfolio − withdrawal ≤ 0 (and the withdrawal > 0) the plan runs out in month e: nothing is paid that month, and every later month holds 0. Otherwise the other assets grow a month (× otherFactor) and pay first, and bitcoin is sold at price[e] for the rest. Lowest = the lowest start-of-month portfolio over months 0 … the run-out month (inclusive), or over the whole path. Capacity: lo = 0, hi = 2 × the monthly spending; if the plan lasts at hi the capacity is hi and hi binds; otherwise, while hi − lo > 10: mid = (lo + hi) ÷ 2, lasting → lo = mid, else hi = mid; the capacity is lo.",
   "inputs": "btc → FireInputs.btc; other → otherUsd; otherFactor → otherMonthlyFactor; monthlyWithdrawal → spendUsd (with retirementIncomeUsd 0, so the withdrawal is the spending); inflation → the yearly rate as a decimal; retireMonth 0; taxRate 0; savingsUsd 0. The months are the path's length.",
   "rowFields": "Each row: [m, btc, other, portfolio, withdrawal, btcSold] — the start of month m, in nominal dollars: btc and other before the month's growth and payment; portfolio = btc × price + other; that month's nominal withdrawal; the coins sold that month. Rows run from month 0 to the run-out month inclusive (the whole path if it lasts).",
   "tolerance": "Rows and lowest: relative 1e-12 (an independent variant that steps the withdrawal by a running factor agrees within 1e-13 — measured). Months, lasts and hiBinds: exact. Capacity: exact — the bisection's midpoints are exact, and every run it decides keeps its tightest month more than $0.25 from the boundary (measured).",
   "fixture": "Round invented figures only — nothing of the Compass. crashFlatRecovery: price[m] = 100000 − 5000m for m ≤ 12; 40000 for 13 ≤ m ≤ 47; 40000 + 1000(m − 47) for m ≥ 48 (240 months). flat50k: 50000 for 24 months.",
   "regenerate": "Only from the reference model, outside the repo (R0) — never from fire.ts. A diff to this file means the reference changed, not the engine."
 },
